							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Lots to counter but one stuck out...<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> I however, just don&#039;t see were it is my responcibility to pay for their mistakes</div><br />Well lets hope any of you all don&#039;t end up in a natural or terrorist disaster with nothing but the clothes on your back.     <br /><br /><br />A couple of things <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">We want help!&quot; uhm.... lets see... I saw few crippled people... there is such a thing as you know... walking? </div> <br /><br />They were told to go and stay there that busses would come to get them.  <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">However, anyone who saw the pictures knows why. Almost every road into New Orleans was destroyed. The ones that weren&#039;t, were damaged, and plugged with debris.<br /><br />Helecopter was about the only was to access the city, </div> <br /><br />That is so untrue you could drive right up to the convention center and the Super dome since day one. <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">That&#039;s the real god damned problem in this country. We all expect instant gratification in our society in all aspects, and many people expect entitlements to said gratifications. It would take weeks to get enough materials and manpower into the city to ahve reinforced those levees strong enough to withstand that storm. </div> <br /><br />Of course not sure why you are bring this up don’t I don’t see anyone complaining that the Army core of engineers didn’t build up the levies in three days before the storm.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">The simple reality is not one thing could have been done to make this less of a disaster in the time frame that the storm was active, and growing. </div> <br /><br />No one is arguing that, they are pissed at the lack of a timely response after the hurricane.  <br /><br />--<br /><br /><br />&nbsp;I see a lot of folks here seeing the TV images of black people on the streets yelling and screaming thinking they must all be welfare, gun-shooting, looting, hooligans. <br /><br />No they are Americans and we Americans help the poor the down trodden the wretched in their time of need.<br /><br />Might need to look deep inside yourselfs, possible you do indeed have a problem. <br /><br /><br /><br /></td>
